        \end{array}\right)=\Th',
        $$ where $\te'=\frac{a\te+b}{c\te+d}.$ Note that for all irrational $\te$, $g\Th$ is well-defined whereas for rational $\te$, $g\Th$ is defined whenever $c\te+d\neq 0.$

        We now consider the particular form of $g=\left(\begin{array}{rr}
        1 & 0 \\
