        C=\left(\begin{array}{cc}
        0 & -c \\
        c & 0
        \end{array}\right), \\
        D=\left(\begin{array}{cc}
        1 & 0 \\
        0 & 1
        \end{array}\right).$$
        Let $\te\in\R$ with $\te\neq-\frac{1}{c}.$ Set $\te'=\frac{\te}{c\te+1}.$ Now we recall the approach of Li \cite{Li04} to find the $A_{\te'}-A_\te$ bimodule.
       % $$C\Theta+D=
        %\left(\begin{array}{cc}
         %c\te+1 & 0 \\
