\section{Conclusion}
In this paper, we propose the Multimodal Representation Decoupling framework (MurreNet) to integrate genomics and pathological WSIs for survival analysis. We innovatively propose MRD module which factorizes modalities into modality-common and modality-specific information to reduce the modality redundancy. To enhance learning constraints, we incorporate a combination of losses for modality similarity, difference, reconstruction and survival prediction task. Finally, we design the DHOF strategy to enable multimodal feature fusion and model the intricate inter- and intra-modality correlations.
Extensive experiments on six TCGA datasets indicate effectiveness of our proposed MurreNet.

