										$Id_{\mathrm{Str\,}}(A\otimes E)\subseteq \ker\varphi$. On the other hand, let $f\in \ker\varphi$, then $f(X_1,\dots,X_m,Y_1,\dots,Y_l)=0$ for the equivariant projections $X_1,\dots,X_m,Y_1,\dots,Y_l$ of $A\otimes\Delta_S$ respecting the $\mathbb{Z}_2$-grading. Therefore for each $m+l$-tuple $(a_1,\ldots,a_{m+l})$ of elements in $A\otimes E$ the equation \[0=f(X_1,\dots,X_m,Y_1,\dots,Y_l)(a_1,\ldots,a_{m+l})=f(a^{(0)}_1,\ldots,a^{(0)}_m,a^{(1)}_{m+1},\ldots, a^{(1)}_{m+l})\] holds, for any elements $a^{(0)}_1,\ldots,a^{(0)}_m$ in $(A\otimes E)^{(0)}$ and $a^{(1)}_{m+1},\ldots, a^{(1)}_{m+l}$ in $(A\otimes E)^{(1)}$. In other words, $f$ is a supertrace identity for $A\otimes E$ and $\ker\varphi=Id_{\mathrm{Str}}(A\otimes E)$.
