\begin{abstract}
We present a proof of a recent conjecture due to M.~Kazarian,
E.~Krasilnikov, S.~Lando, and M.~Shapiro, 
which describes the average value of the universal ${\gl}$-weight system on permutations. The proof uses a quantum analogue of the ${\gl}$-weight system on Hecke algebras of type $A$, which leads to a one-parameter
deformation of the average value of the universal ${\gl}$-weight system. 
We show that the average value of the quantum weight system 
is a linear combination of one-part Schur functions, with
coefficients being $q$-analogues of Bernoulli polynomials.
\end{abstract}

%{\bf AMS Mathematics Subject Classification, 2010:} 05E05, 20C08

{\bf Keywords:} Lie algebra, Hecke algebra, weight system, q-Bernoulli numbers,
Reflection Equation algebra, quantum weight system

