Another potential observable for the identification of NDWP is the electronic dipole moment. As shown in Figure~\ref{fig:Energias}, the Floquet state ${\cal W}^{6}_2$ displays a pronounced Stark shift 
with a positive slope as the driving amplitude increases. This behavior, also observed in planar helium \cite{GonzalezMelan2020}, reflects a large spatial polarization of the electronic density. 
Figure~\ref{fig:Dipolo} shows the expectation value of the dipole operator $\langle x_1 + x_2 \rangle$ for the Floquet eigenstates at fixed field parameters. 
The state ${\cal W}^{6}_2$ (highlighted in red) exhibits the largest dipole moment in the energy window considered, indicating that this quantity could serve as a viable experimental signature for its detection.

