    \caption{The condensate density $|\psi_{\upar(\dar)}|^2$ for different self-interaction strengths: (a) $g = 0.1$, (b) $g = 0.3$, (c) $g = 0.4$, and (d) $g = 0.5.$ Increasing the repulsive interaction causes the condensate to break into multiple fragments, forming several peaks at potential minima located at $x \neq 0$. The other parameters are kept as follows: $V_1 = 1.0$, $V_2 = 0.5$, $k_1 = 0.35$, $k_2/k_1 = (\sqrt{5}-1)/2$, and $\Omega_0 = 0.3.$}
